<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galeazzo Malatesta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1385">1385</a>–<a href="/years/1461">1461</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galeazzo Malatesta, nicknamed 'the Inept', was lord of Pesaro from 1429 to 1445. Burdened by debts and threatened by his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismondo-pandolfo-malatesta">Sigismondo Pandolfo Malatesta</a>, in 1445 he sold Pesaro to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-sforza">Alessandro Sforza</a>, husband of his granddaughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/costanza-da-varano">Costanza da Varano</a>, and Fossombrone to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federico-da-montefeltro">Federico da Montefeltro</a>. The sale ended Malatesta rule in Pesaro.</p></div>
